---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
import { reportUrl } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="What The Editing Lair is, who makes it, and how downloads work." current="about">
  <div class="page">
    <div class="sheet-wrap">
      <article class="sheet doc">
        <h1 class="display doc__title">About</h1>
        <div class="prose">
          <p class="lede">
            The Editing Lair is where Cadenzy publishes the DaVinci Resolve tools he builds for his own edits, alongside
            notes on editing curiosities and tools worth knowing.
          </p>

          <h2>What you will find</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><a href={withBase('plugins/')}>Plugins</a>: Fusion macros for now, with scripts, DCTLs and LUTs possible later.</li>
            <li><a href={withBase('notes/')}>Notes</a>: short posts about editing, Resolve and the tools around it.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>How downloads work</h2>
          <p>
            Free plugins download directly from this site, with no account or sign-up. Every plugin page lists the Resolve
            version and edition it needs and how to install it.
          </p>
          <p>
            Paid plugins are sold through an external store, which handles payment, delivery and receipts. This site never
            asks for payment details.
          </p>

          <h2>Using the plugins</h2>
          <p>
            Free plugins are yours to use in any project, personal or commercial. Please do not
            sell them or share the files themselves; link to the plugin page here instead, so people always get the
            current version.
          </p>

          <h2>Problems and requests</h2>
          <p>
            If a plugin misbehaves, or you have an idea for one, <a href={reportUrl()} rel="noopener">open an issue on
            GitHub</a>. Every plugin page also has a link that fills in the plugin and version for you.
          </p>

          <h2>Notice</h2>
          <p>
            DaVinci Resolve and Fusion are trademarks of Blackmagic Design. The Editing Lair is an independent project and
            is not affiliated with or endorsed by Blackmagic Design.
          </p>
          <p>
            Some covers and preview clips show short excerpts of game trailers to demonstrate an effect. That footage
            belongs to its owners. If you own something shown here and want it removed, <a href={reportUrl()} rel="noopener">open
            an issue</a> and it will be taken down.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    max-width: 960px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 40px var(--gutter) 0;
  }
  .doc {
    padding: clamp(26px, 4vw, 52px) clamp(20px, 5vw, 64px) clamp(36px, 5vw, 64px);
    animation: settle 800ms var(--ease-settle) both;
  }
  .doc__title {
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.75rem);
    color: var(--z0);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.3125rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--z2);
  }
</style>
